WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:04.242
Before trusting a simulation, test its
numerical behavior.

2
00:00:04.723 --> 00:00:07.985
This case follows an AI-assisted investigation

3
00:00:07.985 --> 00:00:12.227
of a beta-DDM bilayer at seventy-five degrees
Celsius.

4
00:00:12.647 --> 00:00:15.809
The original phase diagram marks a lamellar
target

5
00:00:15.809 --> 00:00:17.570
at twenty percent water by mass.

6
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:19.711
That reference guides the question;

7
00:00:20.031 --> 00:00:22.593
the simulation must still establish its
behavior.

8
00:00:23.753 --> 00:00:25.774
The molecular view raises the question

9
00:00:25.774 --> 00:00:27.454
of water inside the membrane.

10
00:00:28.274 --> 00:00:30.675
In the separate single-snapshot analysis,

11
00:00:30.955 --> 00:00:33.396
forty-three waters occupy the local core,

12
00:00:33.776 --> 00:00:36.077
including two in the strict deep subset.

13
00:00:36.637 --> 00:00:39.298
This shows occupancy in one configuration.

14
00:00:39.718 --> 00:00:41.818
It does not establish entry history,

15
00:00:42.139 --> 00:00:45.239
a continuous pore, or complete membrane
crossings.

16
00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.941
The C2 energy slide compares mixed and double
precision

17
00:00:50.281 --> 00:00:52.122
over twenty-five picoseconds,

18
00:00:52.362 --> 00:00:54.582
with the same checkpoint, force field,

19
00:00:54.582 --> 00:00:56.563
and half-femtosecond time step.

20
00:00:56.903 --> 00:00:59.544
Mixed precision shows a large energy loss.

21
00:00:59.844 --> 00:01:03.085
The double-precision trace stays near zero on
this scale,

22
00:01:03.285 --> 00:01:05.285
with small fluctuations remaining.

23
00:01:05.806 --> 00:01:09.226
The reported drift differs by several orders
of magnitude.

24
00:01:10.267 --> 00:01:14.048
The five-picosecond diagnostic table tests
alternatives

25
00:01:14.148 --> 00:01:16.029
from the same prepared checkpoint.

26
00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:19.630
A smaller mixed-precision time step worsens
the drift.

27
00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.150
Tighter LINCS settings remain insufficient.

28
00:01:22.370 --> 00:01:25.331
Leapfrog improves the result but still misses
the screen.

29
00:01:25.671 --> 00:01:28.472
Double precision falls below the stated drift
limit.

30
00:01:28.692 --> 00:01:31.353
These are results for this tested model and
profile,

31
00:01:31.353 --> 00:01:33.573
rather than universal simulation settings.

32
00:01:34.713 --> 00:01:38.396
An earlier matched CPU and MPI comparison

33
00:01:38.656 --> 00:01:41.038
also supports the precision diagnosis.

34
00:01:41.639 --> 00:01:44.101
Its reported whole-box drift is about

35
00:01:44.101 --> 00:01:46.923
three thousand six hundred and seventy-eight
times lower

36
00:01:46.923 --> 00:01:47.964
in double precision.

37
00:01:48.324 --> 00:01:52.047
Rounding during constrained integration is a
plausible contributor.

38
00:01:52.347 --> 00:01:55.510
But the newer C2 tests also changed parallel
layout.

39
00:01:55.790 --> 00:01:58.952
The exact algorithmic contribution remains
unproven.

40
00:01:59.933 --> 00:02:04.875
The tested execution profile uses GROMACS
twenty twenty-four point two,

41
00:02:04.975 --> 00:02:08.097
double precision, and a half-femtosecond time
step.

42
00:02:08.537 --> 00:02:12.819
The thermostat and barostat are off for these
NVE diagnostics.

43
00:02:13.199 --> 00:02:16.080
All four systems pass the unchanged drift
screen

44
00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:17.801
over twenty-five picoseconds.

45
00:02:18.121 --> 00:02:21.222
That addresses numerical conservation in this
test.

46
00:02:21.522 --> 00:02:23.343
Equilibration remains separate:

47
00:02:23.543 --> 00:02:26.945
the slide reports pressure near four thousand
three hundred bar,

48
00:02:27.045 --> 00:02:29.326
and continuing thermal relaxation in C2.

49
00:02:30.767 --> 00:02:33.948
The later water analysis covers twenty
nanoseconds

50
00:02:33.988 --> 00:02:35.808
at seventy-five degrees Celsius.

51
00:02:36.268 --> 00:02:39.449
Its primary local core is the central sixty
percent,

52
00:02:39.629 --> 00:02:43.770
with fixed leaflet identities and a visible
boundary-sensitivity band.

53
00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:47.291
Core occupancy increases during the recorded
window.

54
00:02:48.191 --> 00:02:51.472
Most counted core waters remain close to sugar
headgroups,

55
00:02:51.632 --> 00:02:54.553
while density is much lower near the bilayer
center.

56
00:02:55.393 --> 00:02:57.873
Definitions matter when describing
penetration.

57
00:02:58.873 --> 00:03:01.954
The strict deep subset uses the central forty
percent

58
00:03:01.954 --> 00:03:04.275
and a distance greater than half a nanometre

59
00:03:04.395 --> 00:03:06.115
from the nearest sugar oxygen.

60
00:03:06.475 --> 00:03:09.376
Its plotted mean is zero point three three six

61
00:03:09.376 --> 00:03:10.857
water molecules per frame.

62
00:03:11.457 --> 00:03:12.777
This is a low average,

63
00:03:12.918 --> 00:03:15.938
not zero occupancy or an upper bound on every
frame.

64
00:03:16.379 --> 00:03:19.019
The trace includes frames with four deep
waters.

65
00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:24.063
The original trajectory projections make those
counts visible.

66
00:03:24.544 --> 00:03:27.126
They show two local-core waters initially,

67
00:03:27.386 --> 00:03:29.307
nineteen at ten nanoseconds,

68
00:03:29.348 --> 00:03:31.329
and twenty-four at twenty nanoseconds.

69
00:03:31.709 --> 00:03:34.832
The selected frame at seventeen point six
three nanoseconds

70
00:03:34.832 --> 00:03:36.493
contains four deep waters.

71
00:03:37.014 --> 00:03:38.695
Counts vary across frames.

72
00:03:38.795 --> 00:03:42.358
Projected overlap alone establishes neither a
continuous pore

73
00:03:42.358 --> 00:03:44.399
nor a complete crossing or residence time.

74
00:03:45.420 --> 00:03:48.942
The recorded support message permits a
user-directory build

75
00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:51.503
while central installations are on hold.

76
00:03:51.904 --> 00:03:55.926
The AI agent reports checking cluster
requirements and source checksums,

77
00:03:56.126 --> 00:03:58.928
then preparing a double-precision MPI build

78
00:03:58.928 --> 00:04:01.129
and submitting build and validation jobs.

79
00:04:01.489 --> 00:04:03.950
This illustrates practical workflow
assistance.

80
00:04:04.211 --> 00:04:06.212
The recorded progress report should be read

81
00:04:06.212 --> 00:04:08.673
alongside the actual build and test outputs.

82
00:04:09.613 --> 00:04:12.534
The recording then turns to model
parameterization.

83
00:04:12.954 --> 00:04:17.276
Sobtop supports force-field assignment and
GROMACS topology preparation.

84
00:04:17.696 --> 00:04:20.877
Quantum calculations and charge fitting are
separate steps.

85
00:04:21.137 --> 00:04:23.518
The useful workflow connects these stages

86
00:04:23.718 --> 00:04:25.959
while preserving the source of each parameter

87
00:04:25.959 --> 00:04:27.799
and verifying the assembled model.

88
00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:32.583
The charge-derivation slide begins with
molecular identity:

89
00:04:33.023 --> 00:04:37.146
eighty-one atoms, eighty-two bonds, and ten
stereocentres.

90
00:04:37.847 --> 00:04:41.009
Three gas-phase conformers provide
electrostatic potentials

91
00:04:41.009 --> 00:04:43.150
for a joint, two-stage RESP fit,

92
00:04:43.231 --> 00:04:45.572
with equal weights for the three conformers.

93
00:04:46.033 --> 00:04:49.435
The reported stages converge in seven and six
iterations,

94
00:04:49.435 --> 00:04:51.396
giving a neutral molecular total.

95
00:04:51.937 --> 00:04:55.539
The original table preserves the detailed
method and charge range.

96
00:04:56.740 --> 00:05:00.143
Those new charges are combined with source
GAFF2

97
00:05:00.363 --> 00:05:02.185
bonded and Lennard-Jones terms.

98
00:05:02.465 --> 00:05:04.787
Compatible water and sodium parameters

99
00:05:04.787 --> 00:05:06.709
and the separate phosphate charge models

100
00:05:06.889 --> 00:05:09.491
must remain consistent with the same
conventions.

101
00:05:09.872 --> 00:05:13.434
The source slide explicitly preserves AMBER
scaling

102
00:05:13.635 --> 00:05:15.556
and the original bonded coefficients.

103
00:05:15.737 --> 00:05:19.079
A coherent assembly requires more than a new
set of charges.

104
00:05:20.120 --> 00:05:22.962
The verification slide reports that all

105
00:05:23.082 --> 00:05:26.524
one hundred and ninety-four energy and force
comparisons pass.

106
00:05:27.144 --> 00:05:30.446
The tests cover the molecule, phosphates, and
cross interactions

107
00:05:30.446 --> 00:05:32.808
in separate representations of the same model.

108
00:05:33.368 --> 00:05:36.510
This supports numerical agreement for the
tested configurations.

109
00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:39.972
Experimental force-field accuracy and
equilibrium phase behavior

110
00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.333
remain different questions.

111
00:05:42.413 --> 00:05:44.414
Traceable evidence is the main gain.

112
00:05:44.794 --> 00:05:48.016
The original provenance table links molecular
identity,

113
00:05:48.276 --> 00:05:51.498
charge fitting, parameter sources, and
verification.

114
00:05:52.018 --> 00:05:55.880
The recorded folders also retain preflight
checks and failed attempts.

115
00:05:56.420 --> 00:05:58.601
AI can help organize this work,

116
00:05:58.762 --> 00:06:01.643
but each scientific claim still needs its own
evidence.

117
00:06:02.003 --> 00:06:04.785
Check the numerics, define the water
observable,

118
00:06:04.945 --> 00:06:07.186
and preserve an auditable model history.
